a negative positional keeps every later argument in its slot: true
the trailing argument is still read from slot 3: true
a negative extent is refused, naming the tool, the argument and the value: true
--ocannl_backend=cc    option: true
--bm=64                option: true
--                     option: true
-v                     option: true
-64                    option: false
-0                     option: false
-                      option: false
512                    option: false
f32                    option: false
guard                  option: false
after a lone [--] a flag-looking argument is the positional: true
positionals after [--] keep their slots: true
an ordinary post-[--] argument shadows no setting: true
a post-[--] argument that spells a setting is reported as shadowing it: true
and is still this tool's positional: true
a word positional is read as itself: true
a missing positional falls back to the default: true
a --flag= overrides the positional it duplicates, first spelling winning as in the library: true
without the flag the same slot is still read: true
a documented zero passes under least:0: true
the same zero is refused as an extent: true
a non-integer positional is refused by name: true
a default outside the domain is refused too: true
